Owner turned on Scalable full access (2026-11-07). Trading from chat and calls goes only through a preview card that the owner taps.
- In scope: market and limit buy/sell, plus cancel. Out for now: stop orders, savings plans, watchlist edits, price alerts, suitability warnings on the card.
- No per-order safety limit. Show the preview's expiry countdown on the card.
- Read-only users get a plain "only read access" answer.
- Real-account testing: previews only, never submit. The owner wanted real-account demo videos in the PR too, even though the repo is public.

**Why:** The owner wants the AI to propose and themselves to decide. Scalable's preview proof doesn't prove a human confirmed, so Moneo must hold the submission server-side.
**How to apply:** Never give the model a Scalable submit or cancel tool. Keep new Scalable writes card-only. See [[voice-design-decisions]] (tap-only cards).
